<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $888 mln in August 6 wk.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $888 mln in August 6 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $888 million to $47,564 million in the week ended August 6, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $896 million to $47,851 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $1.717 billion to $874.122 billion.</p>
<p>(( -- Caryn Trokie, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
</text>
